PART 3. STUDENT SUCCESS > CHAPTER III RECOGNITION AND RENEWAL OF STUDENT ORGANIZATIONS > Section 2. Specific Policies
f.
The following are the procedures for selection of Adviser: i.
The student organization submits the names of the prospective adviser attached with the following:
• Adviser's Agreement Form (PNC:SDAS-FO-19); and
• Adviser's Profile Form with 1 x 1 recent picture (PNC:SDAS-FO-17). ii.
The SASD forwards to the Vice President for Student Affairs and Auxiliary Services the names of qualified advisers of student organizations for approval. iii.
The tenure of office of an adviser shall be on a yearly basis subject to renewal after s/he again meets the qualification standards. iv.
His/Her appointment may be terminated after determining the accountability of the erring adviser based on the following grounds:
• Negligence or dereliction of duty;
• Abuse of authority;
• Embezzlement of funds;
• Disgraceful or immoral conduct;
• Sexual harassment;
• Illegal collection of funds;
• Gross inefficiency or incompetence;
• Tampering or falsification of documents; and
• Commission or conviction of a crime. g.
The following are the functions of Adviser: i.
Assist the organization in planning and periodic evaluation of its programs and activities; ii.
Serve as primary resource person of the organization, especially in its effort to achieve its plans and activities as well as in training and other developmental activities; iii.
Help the individual members recognize issues and concerns and process them to resolve in the most appropriate manner; iv.
Review all written communications, requests, project proposals, and give initial approval to the activities of the organization;
v.
Accompany the organization in all its official in-person and remote external activities; vi.

